# Line endings.
#
# Windows editors save CRLF; Linux and macOS save LF. Without this file Git
# stores whatever it is handed, so a file merely re-saved on Windows shows up
# as "every line changed" in the diff. That is noise in a pull request, and
# noise in a pull request is how a real change gets waved through unread.
#
#   text=auto  Git decides what is text and normalizes it to LF in the repo
#   eol=lf     and checks it back out as LF everywhere, Windows included
*       text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted. Listing them now is cheap
# insurance for when source PDFs and screenshots land in the repo.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
